{"task_id": "HumanEval/37", "solution": "```python\ndef sort_even(l: list):\n    \"\"\"This function takes a list l and returns a list l' such that\n    l' is identical to l in the odd indicies, while its values at the even indicies are equal\n    to the values of the even indicies of l, but sorted.\n    \"\"\"\n    even_elements = []\n    for i in range(len(l)):\n        if i % 2 == 0:\n            even_elements.append(l[i])\n\n    even_elements.sort()\n\n    result_list = list(l) # Initialize result_list as a copy to retain original odd-indexed elements\n    sorted_even_idx = 0\n\n    for i in range(len(l)):\n        if i % 2 == 0:\n            result_list[i] = even_elements[sorted_even_idx]\n            sorted_even_idx += 1\n        # Odd-indexed elements are already correctly placed from the initial copy.\n\n    return result_list\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/38", "solution": "```python\ndef decode_cyclic(s: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Decodes a string that was encoded with the encode_cyclic function.\n    It reverses the left cyclic shift for groups of three characters.\n    \"\"\"\n    decoded_parts = []\n    n = len(s)\n    for i in range(0, n, 3):\n        group = s[i:i+3]\n        if len(group) == 3:\n            # Reverse the left cyclic shift: 'bca' becomes 'abc' by moving the last char to the front.\n            decoded_group = group[2] + group[0:2]\n            decoded_parts.append(decoded_group)\n        else:\n            # Groups shorter than 3 characters were not modified, so they remain unchanged.\n            decoded_parts.append(group)\n    return \"\".join(decoded_parts)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/38", "solution": "```python\ndef decode_cyclic(s: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    takes as input string encoded with encode_cyclic function. Returns decoded string.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Split string into groups of three, identical to encode_cyclic.\n    groups = [s[(3 * i):min((3 * i + 3), len(s))] for i in range((len(s) + 2) // 3)]\n\n    # Reverse the cyclic shift for groups of three characters; others remain unchanged.\n    decoded_groups = [\n        (group[-1] + group[:-1]) if len(group) == 3 else group\n        for group in groups\n    ]\n\n    # Join the processed groups to form the final decoded string.\n    return \"\".join(decoded_groups)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/40", "solution": "```python\ndef triples_sum_to_zero(l: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    triples_sum_to_zero takes a list of integers as an input.\n    it returns True if there are three distinct elements in the list that\n    sum to zero, and False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(l) < 3:\n        return False\n\n    l.sort()\n\n    n = len(l)\n    for i in range(n - 2):\n        if i > 0 and l[i] == l[i-1]:\n            continue\n\n        left_pointer = i + 1\n        right_pointer = n - 1\n        target_sum_for_two_pointers = -l[i]\n\n        while left_pointer < right_pointer:\n            current_two_sum = l[left_pointer] + l[right_pointer]\n\n            if current_two_sum == target_sum_for_two_pointers:\n                return True\n            elif current_two_sum < target_sum_for_two_pointers:\n                left_pointer += 1\n            else:\n                right_pointer -= 1\n\n    return False\n```"}
