{"task_id": "HumanEval/19", "solution": "```python\ndef sort_numbers(numbers: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Input is a space-delimited string of numberals from 'zero' to 'nine'.\n    Returns the string with numbers sorted from smallest to largest.\"\"\"\n    word_to_int_map = {\n        'zero': 0, 'one': 1, 'two': 2, 'three': 3, 'four': 4,\n        'five': 5, 'six': 6, 'seven': 7, 'eight': 8, 'nine': 9\n    }\n    int_to_word_map = [\n        'zero', 'one', 'two', 'three', 'four',\n        'five', 'six', 'seven', 'eight', 'nine'\n    ]\n\n    # Split the input string into individual number words\n    number_words = numbers.split(' ')\n\n    # Convert words to their integer representations\n    integer_numbers = [word_to_int_map[word] for word in number_words]\n\n    # Sort the list of integers\n    integer_numbers.sort()\n\n    # Convert the sorted integers back to their word representations\n    sorted_number_words = [int_to_word_map[num] for num in integer_numbers]\n\n    # Join the sorted words back into a space-delimited string\n    return ' '.join(sorted_number_words)\n```"}
